==Strategy==
This stage may seem challenging due the overwhelming number of Iron Claw X's, however their single target can be abused in your favour, allowing you to spam many meatshields to stall the "onslaught" on more effectively, meanwhile using long distance area attackers such as [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Crimson Mina]] or [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] to chip the 7 bosses down. Due to the presence of Pigeon de Sable, a wave blocker such as [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] may be necessary to prevent its waves from destroying your meatshield stack.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] - Can block waves from Pigeon de Sable, thus stopping units behind him.
*[[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Crimson Mina]] - Mina can be used to deal damage from a safe distance and can be used with meatshields to deal damage with no threats besides the Metal Doges and Pigeon de Sables.
*Most spammable units work well here, as they trigger Iron Claw Xs Single Attack and stop him from dealing damage to your backliners.
*[[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]] - Can single-handedly deal with the entire threat of the Metal Doges, but requires constant meatshielding due to his short range.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Most Long-Distance Ubers (e.g. [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Megaphrodite]] or [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli, Daughter of Chaos]]) work well here, as they are able to deal damage from a safe distance while still helping clear out peons.

